single thing but doing it right.   This  section  outlines  which
these  components  are.  Public utilities: Executes a command and
checks that its exit code, its standard output and  its  standard
error output match pre‐specified expected values.  Queries static
configuration  information.   Converts  the  output  of  to user‐
friendly and/or machine‐parseable reports.  Automates the  execu‐
tion of a series of test programs and collects their results in a
unified report.  Shell interpreter for shell‐based test programs.
Programming  interfaces:  C  programming  interface for test pro‐
grams.  C++ programming interface for test programs.  POSIX shell
programming interface for test programs.  Other:  Description  of
the  machine‐parseable  data  formats used by the tools.  Generic
description of test cases, independent of the language  they  are
implemented  in.   Common interface provided by the test programs
